    <section id="section-1">
        <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
        <p>The App is provided by <strong>Maoxia Xiang</strong> ("we", "us", or "our"). For privacy questions, contact us using the details in <a href="#section-13">Section 13</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="section-2">
        <h2>2. Our Core Privacy Principle</h2>
        <p>The App is designed to work <strong>without collecting your personal information</strong>. We do not require an account, and we do not operate servers that receive your content or usage data.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="section-3">
        <h2>3. Information We Process</h2>
        
        <h3>3.1 Local Storage (Default)</h3>
        <p>Photos and videos you import are stored at original quality inside the App's private sandbox on your device. The App also generates thumbnails locally and stores the albums, tags, custom names, pinned status, and sort order you create in a local database. <strong>This data stays on your device, is never transmitted to us, and is never shared with third parties.</strong></p>

        <h3>3.2 Photo Library Access</h3>
        <p>To import media, the App requests permission to access your system photo library only when you actively choose to import. This permission is used solely to read the items you select. If you enable <em>"Delete original from system photo library after import,"</em> the App deletes the corresponding original locally on your device after a successful import.</p>

        <h3>3.3 iCloud Sync (Optional, Pro Feature)</h3>
        <p>If you enable iCloud Sync, the App uses Apple's CloudKit private database to sync your album data across your own devices. This data is stored in your iCloud account, governed by the Apple Privacy Policy, and we have no access to it. You can disable sync at any time.</p>

        <h3>3.4 In-App Purchases</h3>
        <p>Pro is unlocked through Apple App Store In-App Purchase. All payments are processed by Apple; we do not collect or receive your payment details. We only read Apple-provided purchase records to determine your Pro entitlement.</p>

        <h3>3.5 What We Do Not Collect</h3>
        <p>The App contains <strong>no third-party analytics, advertising, crash-reporting, or tracking SDKs</strong>. We do not collect your name, email, phone number, location, contacts, or device identifiers for tracking, and we do not profile you or use your data for advertising.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="section-4">
        <h2>4. Legal Bases for Processing (UK / EEA)</h2>
        <p>Because we do not collect or process personal data on our own servers, no legal basis under the UK GDPR or EU GDPR is generally engaged by us. To the extent any processing occurs (for example, on-device features you initiate), it is based on your <strong>consent</strong> and/or the <strong>performance of our agreement with you</strong>, and you may withdraw consent at any time by discontinuing the relevant feature.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="section-5">
        <h2>5. Disclosure of Information</h2>
        <p>We do not disclose your personal information to third parties. We may disclose information only if required by law — however, because your content remains on your device, <strong>we generally have nothing to disclose.</strong></p>
    </section>

    <section id="section-6">
        <h2>6. No Sale or Sharing of Personal Information</h2>
        <p>We <strong>do not sell</strong> and <strong>do not share</strong> your personal information, including as those terms are defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA) and similar U.S. state laws. We do not engage in targeted advertising.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="section-7">
        <h2>7. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table>
